# PinGen - Pinterest Automation SaaS

## Project Overview
You are building PinGen, a Pinterest automation SaaS that helps users create, schedule, and optimize Pinterest content at scale.

## Tech Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 14 App Router (React 18+)
- **Language**: TypeScript (strict mode enabled)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 3.4+
- **UI Components**: shadcn/ui
- **Backend**: Supabase (Auth, Database, Storage)
- **Payments**: Stripe
- **Deployment**: Vercel

## Architecture Rules

### Component Types
- **Server Components by default** - Use async components for data fetching
- **Client Components only when necessary** - Add 'use client' directive only for:
  - Interactive UI (buttons, forms, modals)
  - Browser APIs (localStorage, clipboard)
  - Real-time features
  - Third-party client-side libraries

### API Routes
- All API routes use **Edge Runtime**
- Error handling: Always return `{ data, error }` shape, never throw
- Use typed request/response with Zod validation

### TypeScript Rules
- **No `any` types** - Always infer or define explicit types
- Use `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/complex types
- Export types from `src/types/` directory
- Use satisfies operator for config objects

## Design System

### Colors
- **Primary (Pinterest Red)**: `#E3001B`
- **Primary Hover**: `#C40018`
- **Background**: `#FFFFFF`
- **Surface**: `#F7F7F7`
- **Border**: `#E2E2E2`
- **Text Primary**: `#111111`
- **Text Secondary**: `#717171`
- **Text Muted**: `#9CA3AF`
- **Success**: `#22C55E`
- **Warning**: `#F59E0B`

### Typography
- **Headings**: Inter, font-weight 700
- **Body**: Inter, font-weight 400
- **Small/UI**: Inter, font-weight 500

### Spacing
- Use Tailwind spacing scale (4 = 1rem = 16px)
- Section padding: py-20 (80px vertical)
- Container max-width: max-w-7xl (1280px)
- Card padding: p-6 (24px)

## File Structure
```
src/
├── app/                    # Next.js App Router
│   ├── (marketing)/        # Marketing pages (landing, pricing)
│   ├── (dashboard)/        # App dashboard (protected)
│   ├── api/                # API routes
│   └── layout.tsx          # Root layout
├── components/
│   ├── ui/                 # shadcn/ui components
│   ├── landing/            # Landing page sections
│   ├── dashboard/          # Dashboard components
│   └── shared/             # Shared components
├── hooks/                  # Custom React hooks
├── lib/                    # Utilities, configs
│   ├── utils.ts            # cn() and helpers
│   ├── supabase.ts         # Supabase client
│   └── stripe.ts           # Stripe config
├── types/                  # TypeScript types
└── styles/                 # Global styles
```

## Naming Conventions
- **Components**: PascalCase (e.g., `PinGenerator.tsx`)
- **Hooks**: camelCase with use prefix (e.g., `usePins.ts`)
- **Utils**: camelCase (e.g., `formatDate.ts`)
- **Types**: PascalCase with suffix (e.g., `PinType.ts`)
- **Constants**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE

## Code Patterns

### Component Template
```tsx
// Server component (default)
interface ComponentProps {
  title: string;
  children: React.ReactNode;
}

export function Component({ title, children }: ComponentProps) {
  return (
    <div className="...">
      <h2>{title}</h2>
      {children}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Client Component Template
```tsx
'use client';

import { useState } from 'react';

interface InteractiveProps {
  initialCount: number;
}

export function Interactive({ initialCount }: InteractiveProps) {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(initialCount);
  
  return (
    <button onClick={() => setCount(c => c + 1)}>
      Count: {count}
    </button>
  );
}
```

### API Route Template
```tsx
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from 'next/server';
import { z } from 'zod';

const requestSchema = z.object({
  pinId: z.string().uuid(),
});

export async function POST(request: NextRequest) {
  try {
    const body = await request.json();
    const { pinId } = requestSchema.parse(body);
    
    // Business logic here
    const data = await processPin(pinId);
    
    return NextResponse.json({ data, error: null });
  } catch (error) {
    return NextResponse.json(
      { data: null, error: error.message },
      { status: 400 }
    );
  }
}
```

## Performance Rules
- Use `next/image` for all images
- Lazy load below-fold sections
- Use `loading="lazy"` for iframes
- Minimize client-side JavaScript
- Use Server Components for data fetching

## Accessibility
- All images have descriptive alt text
- Interactive elements have focus states
- Color contrast ratio >= 4.5:1
- Support keyboard navigation
- Use semantic HTML elements

